    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "810004b4_509722d3",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-27T17:16:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider this alternative (both here, and throughout the file):\n\n   return {WifiStatusCode::SUCCESS, \"\"};\n\nNow that hidl_string has a copying conversion constructor, I think we really only need createWifiStatus() when we\u0027re mapping from a legacy error.\n\n(Strictly speaking, I think this particular case could have been handled before the copying conversion constructor, with |{WifiStatusCode::SUCCESS, {}}|. But it wouldn\u0027t have made much sense to switch to this style for just one case. Now, we can use this more compact style for all cases where we\u0027re not dealing with legacy errors.)",
      "revId": "ae5ffdd7fa058301855b01fee935af88a35a9f0d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "81ce44ee_cf4c2e40",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
